# Security

Every endpoint, upload, message, payment, AI call, and GPS write assumes hostile input.

## Requirements

- Authentication / authorization / sessions / permissions validated server-side
- Tokens hashed at rest when stored (portal); secrets compared with constant-time helpers
- API routes: JWT or signed webhook / hook secret — never trust client money or entitlement fields
- Uploads: private storage + uid path; validate size/type
- Payments: signature verification + idempotency; settle only on captured funds
- AI: ownership + money sanitize; never trust client business snapshots or unbounded actions
- GPS / location: minimize retention; treat as sensitive PII
- Secrets only in server env; never `VITE_` for private keys
- Security headers (CSP, HSTS, frame deny) via platform config
- Rate limit auth, OTP, OCR, AI, mail, billing hooks
- Validate + sanitize + filter inputs; encode outputs; allowlist deep links
- Defend CSRF (SameSite + CORS allowlist), XSS, SQLi (parameterized / PostgREST), prompt injection
- Abuse / brute-force / replay: rate limits, OTP attempt caps, webhook idempotency
- Log safely (redact secrets); monitor webhooks and privilege paths; alert on spikes

## Definition of done

Incomplete if a client can escalate privileges, mark money settled, inject prompts that change facts, open-redirect via notifications, or burn paid APIs without auth/rate limits.
